WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.612
Step four exports the open incidents.

2
00:00:02.612 --> 00:00:07.930
The filter asks for incidents whose status
is active, and the export keeps the I D,

3
00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:12.200
the name, the severity, who it's
assigned to, and when it was created.

4
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:16.362
The second command reads the file
back, so you can see the owner column.

5
00:00:16.362 --> 00:00:19.738
The guide's pass: every
open incident has an owner.

6
00:00:19.738 --> 00:00:22.876
Step five exports one
incident with its alerts.

7
00:00:22.876 --> 00:00:25.575
Use an incident number
from step four's output.

8
00:00:25.575 --> 00:00:29.352
Microsoft Learn's page shows
the expand property for alerts,

9
00:00:29.352 --> 00:00:33.581
so the file carries every alert in
the incident and its evidence, and,

10
00:00:33.581 --> 00:00:37.962
once the incident is resolved, its
classification and determination.

11
00:00:37.962 --> 00:00:41.625
That file is what an assessor
traces from alert to closure.

12
00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:43.163
Step six backs it out.

13
00:00:43.163 --> 00:00:46.351
Nothing changed in the tenant,
so you only disconnect.

14
00:00:46.351 --> 00:00:49.630
Keep the evidence folder with
the rest of the path's files.
